{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-029c7222-74ae-4b6d-80cf-96c578360f2f","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-b7a1f87e0ead1ddc","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9003-bmvve6ms/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9003-E001.md","content":"# Ship 8-hour default workbench idle culling timeout\n\n## Description\n\nChange the shipped default workbench idle culling timeout from 24 hours to 8\nhours so that newly installed clusters stop idle workbenches after 8 hours\nwithout any admin action. The idle culler, its ConfigMap, and the Dashboard\nadministration UI already exist; this change only moves the shipped default\nvalue. Clusters that already have an explicitly configured idle culling\ntimeout keep their configured value on upgrade.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Change the default idle culling timeout shipped for newly installed clusters\n  from 24 hours to 8 hours in the notebook-controller culler configuration\n  (`notebook-controller-culler-config` ConfigMap default), so a cluster with no\n  explicitly configured value culls workbenches idle for 8 hours.\n- Preserve upgrade behavior: clusters with an explicitly configured idle\n  culling timeout are not modified when upgrading to the release carrying the\n  new default.\n- Validate that the existing Dashboard cluster-settings administration UI\n  correctly reflects the new default and still allows admins to override it\n  (no Dashboard code changes — the UI and setting already exist).\n- Update the release note and the cluster-settings documentation to state the\n  new 8-hour default and how to override it.\n\nOut of scope (per strategy): per-project or per-user culling policies, and any\nchanges to activity detection (kernel probe behavior).\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a newly installed cluster with no explicitly configured idle culling\n  timeout, when a workbench has been idle for 8 hours, then it is culled\n  (stopped) — measured by the shipped culler configuration default being 8\n  hours.\n- Given a cluster upgraded from a previous release that has an explicitly\n  configured idle culling timeout, when the upgrade completes, then the\n  configured value is unchanged — measured by the pre-upgrade and\n  post-upgrade configured values matching.\n- Given the Dashboard cluster-settings administration UI, when an admin views\n  or edits the idle culling settings, then the 8-hour default is surfaced\n  correctly and overriding it still works — measured by manual verification\n  through the existing administration UI.\n- Given the release notes and cluster-settings documentation, when the change\n  ships, then they state the new 8-hour default and describe how to override\n  it — measured by documentation review.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **HLR-1 (P1)**: Default idle culling timeout for newly installed clusters is\n  8 hours; existing clusters with an explicitly configured value are not\n  changed on upgrade — covered by the default change, upgrade-preservation\n  scope, and the first two acceptance criteria.\n- **HLR-2 (P2)**: Release note and cluster-settings documentation state the\n  new default and how to override it — covered by the documentation update in\n  scope and the final acceptance criterion.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":25799,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b30e8d9c1b6fd804","agent_id":"a45fe0d08e5e7727c","session_id":"e63dac3f-6cb8-4b42-a04f-a78da24c0b54","uuid":"168d61ce-98b8-4896-b25e-025be2d872f9","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:14:49.221Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9003"}
