{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9934fafab92f833a","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9003-E001\n3\ttitle: Ship 8-hour default workbench idle culling timeout\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9003\n5\tcomponent: Notebooks\n6\tteam: Workbenches\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 1\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 1\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 0\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 7\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Ship 8-hour default workbench idle culling timeout\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tChange the shipped default workbench idle culling timeout from 24 hours to 8\n34\thours so that newly installed clusters stop idle workbenches after 8 hours\n35\twithout any admin action. The idle culler, its ConfigMap, and the Dashboard\n36\tadministration UI already exist; this change only moves the shipped default\n37\tvalue. Clusters that already have an explicitly configured idle culling\n38\ttimeout keep their configured value on upgrade.\n39\t\n40\t## Scope\n41\t\n42\t- Change the default idle culling timeout shipped for newly installed clusters\n43\t  from 24 hours to 8 hours in the notebook-controller culler configuration\n44\t  (`notebook-controller-culler-config` ConfigMap default), so a cluster with no\n45\t  explicitly configured value culls workbenches idle for 8 hours.\n46\t- Preserve upgrade behavior: clusters with an explicitly configured idle\n47\t  culling timeout are not modified when upgrading to the release carrying the\n48\t  new default.\n49\t- Validate that the existing Dashboard cluster-settings administration UI\n50\t  correctly reflects the new default and still allows admins to override it\n51\t  (no Dashboard code changes — the UI and setting already exist).\n52\t- Update the release note and the cluster-settings documentation to state the\n53\t  new 8-hour default and how to override it.\n54\t\n55\tOut of scope (per strategy): per-project or per-user culling policies, and any\n56\tchanges to activity detection (kernel probe behavior).\n57\t\n58\t## Acceptance Criteria\n59\t\n60\t- Given a newly installed cluster with no explicitly configured idle culling\n61\t  timeout, when a workbench has been idle for 8 hours, then it is culled\n62\t  (stopped) — measured by the shipped culler configuration default being 8\n63\t  hours.\n64\t- Given a cluster upgraded from a previous release that has an explicitly\n65\t  configured idle culling timeout, when the upgrade completes, then the\n66\t  configured value is unchanged — measured by the pre-upgrade and\n67\t  post-upgrade configured values matching.\n68\t- Given the Dashboard cluster-settings administration UI, when an admin views\n69\t  or edits the idle culling settings, then the 8-hour default is surfaced\n70\t  correctly and overriding it still works — measured by manual verification\n71\t  through the existing administration UI.\n72\t- Given the release notes and cluster-settings documentation, when the change\n73\t  ships, then they state the new 8-hour default and describe how to override\n74\t  it — measured by documentation review.\n75\t\n76\t## HLR Traceability\n77\t\n78\t- **HLR-1 (P1)**: Default idle culling timeout for newly installed clusters is\n79\t  8 hours; existing clusters with an explicitly configured value are not\n80\t  changed on upgrade — covered by the default change, upgrade-preservation\n81\t  scope, and the first two acceptance criteria.\n82\t- **HLR-2 (P2)**: Release note and cluster-settings documentation state the\n83\t  new default and how to override it — covered by the documentation update in\n84\t  scope and the final acceptance criterion.\n85\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-ad340eeeeefad80a","agent_id":"a04a93eac4114fd64","session_id":"e63dac3f-6cb8-4b42-a04f-a78da24c0b54","uuid":"e8fe2e1f-fef4-4798-9204-dd005d614152","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:16:45.352Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9934fafab92f833a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9003 decomposition"}
