criteria, each in given/when/then form with an explicit measurement (shipped config default value, pre/post-upgrade value match, manual verification through the existing UI, documentation review). The HLR-1 upgrade-preservation clause is captured as a dedicated AC. No rule-mandated ACs apply: this is not a component replacement (no rollback/feature-flag AC required), not a `docs-authoring` epic, and not part of a konflux chain. The epic body does not reference sibling epics by draft ID.\n38\t\n39\t### 7. Completeness (2/2)\n40\tAll strategy scope is accounted for in E001: the default change, upgrade preservation, Dashboard UI validation, and the HLR-2 release-note/cluster-settings documentation updates. Out-of-scope items (per-project/per-user culling policies, kernel probe changes) are correctly carried into the epic's out-of-scope note. The strategy has no Prerequisites & Process Gates section declaring documentation support, so no separate `docs-authoring` epic is required; the incidental doc touch-ups stay in the single epic per the below-threshold path. No conditional branches are needed (no bounded unknowns), and strategy-level context (no open questions, no risks requiring carry-forward) is handled.\n41\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-a43dd41c771bdfad","agent_id":"ab159acc69e45b81a","session_id":"e63dac3f-6cb8-4b42-a04f-a78da24c0b54","uuid":"fe588a5f-ac76-4690-9a23-e53b96b27fd6","timestamp":"2026-10-21T23:19:48.702Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-9be2e05a0167461a","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-9003 decomposition"}
